{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition","id":783480,"title":"Sell Me on Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-10T09:33:43-08:00","id":783480,"title":"Sell Me on Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition","content":"Back when the Wraith 20th KS came out, Hawthorn, created a 'Sell me Wraith' as he had done before for M20 and during that expressed that he wouldn't do it again for C20. I, however, said that I would because of the five original game lines, CtD was the only one that I never touched.<br /> <br /> So I ask you Changeling fans, sell me and those like me on C20, sell me on Changeling: the Dream. Don't bring up Dark Ages: Fae or Changeling: the Lost, CtD should stand up on its own merits, not those of others. Consider me someone that has never touched any of the Changeling/Fae games of WW/OPP.<br /> <br /> Why should I, someone with no experience with the line, back C20?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T09:43:15-08:00","id":783486,"title":"","content":"I'm supposed to be at work, so excuse the stream of consciousness here. So...<br /> <br /> All of White Wolfs games offer up a lot of feels. To me though Changeling is a game that offers a very specific feeling, the feeling of holding onto your childhood. Keeping it safe and warm from all the slings and arrows of life. I think we as role players do this every day more than just about any other group, and it's rare to find a game that so wonderfully touches on those themes. I think anyone who loves our hobby can love Changeling the Dreaming, and if they get into it, it will truly touch them on some primal level virtually no other game can. Just food for thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T17:48:36-08:00","id":784439,"title":"","content":"I just think it's the best game for running urban fantasy like Neil Gaiman, Charles de Lint and others. It can be dark, but it doesn't need to be (like Mage). It is set in the World of Darkness, but has its own fantasy world to explore with its own politics and rewards (like Wraith). It allows you to have raging fantasy battles on the streets without breaching the Masquerade or gaining Paradox (so long as it's entirely chimerical). It's just, generally, a very versatile game, and allows for archetypal quests, politics and intrigue, and wonder or despair all at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T07:36:09-08:00","id":784730,"title":"","content":"CtD is a game abou geeks/nerds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/571-nin","name":"Nin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T11:26:23-08:00","id":784867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=784730#post784730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CtD is a game abou geeks/nerds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you please explain? You could make a similar argument about Mage (which is about people trying to understand how the universe works, and in Ascension they go about it the wrong way in order to make such a great setting).<br /> <br /> <br /> For my view, bare in mind I haven't had an opportunity to play it, Changeling is a game about Hope, Wonder, Despair, and Normalcy. Broadly speaking the first two are better than the latter two, but it's not strictly the case. CtD is about balancing the fact you're an ordinary person with the fact that you're a reincarnated fairy, and the two don't always align, but they don't always clash. It's about losing yourself in wonder, but keeping a link to the mundane so that you don't go crazy.<br /> <br /> Bare in mind that this isn't explained very well in the mechanics, but it's useful to have some Banality so you don't just saunter off into the Dreaming and become crazy as your Glamour grows, but it's also a good idea not to have too much, or else you'll become a normal human.<br /> <br /> At least, that's why, as somebody who has never proper experienced it, would back CtD20 if I wasn't a poor student. As it is I'll be buying the cheapest physical rulebook I can when they come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T15:10:26-08:00","id":785010,"title":"","content":"I've been lukewarm about C20 until I read:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=784439#post784439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think it's the best game for running urban fantasy like Neil Gaiman, Charles de Lint and others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I an reminded why I love changeling again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T11:14:58-08:00","id":790934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=784867#post784867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you please explain? You could make a similar argument about Mage (which is about people trying to understand how the universe works, and in Ascension they go about it the wrong way in order to make such a great setting).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can try, though I wouldn't have used the words Nin used.<br /> Changeling the Dreaming is a game where your character (we'll call him Steve) opens his eyes one day and realises that he's not an office worker at Jobson and Co, but rather that he's a magical prince from the dreamland of Arcadia, with mystic powers and ancient romance and all that, and that his boss isn't really Mr. Jobson, the middle manager in third generation, but rather an evil alien monster that came to our world to eat Imagination and promote Soul Crushing Despair of Office Life. So Steve takes his Sword of Glory (which boring muggles see as his old golf club) and goes on to slay dragons and beat Mr. Jobson to death or something. And then you go and have a creepy romance with a Sidhe princess in the body of a ten year old girl.<br /> <br /> Also Tony Diterlizzi's art is pretty good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T00:39:00-08:00","id":791403,"title":"","content":"One of the nice things about <b>Changeling: the Dreaming </b>is that it lets you play with concepts and locations that just don't work anywhere else, and that would radically change the World of Darkness if allowed to spread to the other lines. Ice castles and talking polar bears? Check. Underground cities populated by man-eating dark elves? Check. Baseball gnomes? Check.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Dreaming&quot; is a spirit realm built out of humanity's collective subconscious - anything humanity's ever fantasized about, wrote about, or woken screaming from a nightmare over, exists <i>somewhere</i> in the Dreaming. And unlike the Shadowlands or the Umbra, the Dreaming still directly touches the Earth. It overlays everything, pooling into coherent fantasy realms that exist simultaneously with more mundane elements of reality.<br /> <br /> Players take on the role of spirit beings from the Dreaming who've merged themselves with humanity to survive in the modern era. Exactly what they were before is left ambiguous, but changelings* (the default cultural block) believe they were the fairies of European myth. The Seelie and Unseelie Courts, high elves, goblins and dwarves, giants and ogres . . . They all live on, wrapped in human flesh and shielded by the soul they've merged with.<br /> <br /> Left to their own devices, modern changelings tend to default to an Arthurian, vaguely Celtic feel. But in places where the local Dreaming has a strong theme of its own, long term residents adopt roles within the local mythos. New York City is steampunk, for example, while the changelings of Boston are busy reenacting the American Revolution. Changelings are born of the Dreaming, after all, and they instinctively play the parts humanity has dreamt for them.<br /> <br /> The game line debuted at a lull in the metaplot. For centuries, the only sidhe (high elves) on Earth were House Scathach and the occasional Lost One - both rare enough that many changelings believed the sidhe were gone or even extinct. But in the wake of the moon landing, when the imagination of virtually every human was aflame, five entire Houses of sidhe rode out of the heart of the Dreaming . . . and promptly plunged the changeling world into civil war, as they tried to reassert control.<br /> <br /> In modern days, the rise of High King David (a sidhe with strong ties to the &quot;commoner&quot; changelings) has resulted in an uneasy peace . . . a peace that may have arrived too late to save the changelings. Winter is coming. Humanity continues to turn from the wonder of imagination, from the Dreaming itself, slowly starving the changelings of the Glamour they need to survive.<br /> <br /> And yet they fight on. As the world grows darker, vampires whisper of Gehenna and werewolves fear the Apocalypse, the changelings ready for war. The smithies of nockers ring with song as they beat dragon scale into armor, and forge moonlight into blades. If this is to be the end of the world, the changelings intend their last stand to be one worthy of legend. As the darkness rises, the children of dreams make ready to fight alongside the humans who breathed life into them.<br /> <br /> (And yet many sidhe are haunted by a nagging sense that they've forgotten something important . . . Why were so many of them wounded, when they first arrived on Earth? Why are their dreams haunted by vague memories of palaces in flames, and desperate war councils?)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * their Native American counterparts (the nunnehi), or Asian (the hsien), tell very different stories about their origins. But &quot;overlapping&quot; groups like the menehune imply that (fundamentally) they're the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=784730#post784730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CtD is a game abou geeks/nerds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think I would've compared it to LARPing. Even more so than the werewolves, changelings (et al) are dual-natured beings. They exist simultaneously as humans and faerie creatures, they are continually aware of both mundane Earth and the Dreaming . . . both are real for them.<br /> <br /> And yet the humans around them are blind and ignorant to the Dreaming side of things. Thus changelings dealing with &quot;chimerical' beings or other problems within the Dreaming often seem to be play acting or miming to humans. Coupled with &quot;interesting&quot; fashion choices, a group of changelings often look like refugees from an SCA reenactment engaging in LARP. And those are the lucky ones. Unlucky ones often get institutionalized as being mentally ill - ranting and raving about beings the humans can't see, afflicted with problems that aren't &quot;real&quot;. A chimerically broken leg is still broken . . . for a changeling, but it won't show up on an X-ray.<br /> <br /> Now, changelings are free to ignore the Dreaming, deny that its real . . . but that has consequences, too. The faerie half of their soul starts to fall asleep, starts to forget who and what it is. Deny the Dreaming too long, and you may not be able to find your way back to it. Are you still a LARPer (or geek/nerd) if you never game, never go to the cons, never read another fantasy novel or watched another sci-fi show? That's the problem changelings face. Pretend too hard, and the lie becomes real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":".  typo 12-23-2015, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T00:53:24-08:00","id":791411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (And yet many sidhe are haunted by a nagging sense that they've forgotten something important . . . Why were so many of them wounded, when they first arrived on Earth? Why are their dreams haunted by vague memories of palaces in flames, and desperate war councils?) </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure we know the answer - the Technocracy curbstomped them, and then curbstomped them again on the moon, to make the whole moon landing thing and get a piece of space into the Consensus.<br /> And the reason Technocracy (and everyone else) is able to mop up the floor with the Changelings because all the Changeling swords and dragons and rings of power aren't real. They are glamours, existing only in the Dreaming. A Changeling can spend some of his magic to materialized the items for a short time, but that comes with another set of problems. Changelings can do some scary and interesting things (Sidhe can run around with Appearance 10), but they burn out <i>very</i> quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T16:46:27-08:00","id":792429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=784867#post784867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you please explain?</div> </div> </div> </div>First: Sam Chupp said (Darker Days Radio #25 or so?) CtD is something like a loveletter to geeks/nerds. So, to be correct I should have wrote: &quot;CtD is a game <b>to</b> geeks/nerds.&quot;<br /> Second: Kithain in CtD are adults (ignoring Childlings) who never really grow up ... when they do they are lost to banality.<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SeNpwWIp7t0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SeNpwWIp7t0</a> 1:20:33","signature":"","edited":{"userid":571,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/571-nin","user":"Nin","date":". 12-24-2015, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/571-nin","name":"Nin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T10:55:24-08:00","id":793194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=792429#post792429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second: Kithain in CtD are adults (ignoring Childlings) who never really grow up ... when they do they are lost to banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm calling your bluff. Childlings are from 3 to 13 years old, Wildlings are from 13 to 25, and Grumps are 25+. However, playing a Grump is like dying in chargen, since your massive Banality score is deadly. So the best you are going to manage is being an 18 y.o. Wildling. Childlings being mechanically optimal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T14:47:06-08:00","id":793276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=791403#post791403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the nice things about <b>Changeling: the Dreaming </b>is that it lets you play with concepts and locations that just don't work anywhere else, and that would radically change the World of Darkness if allowed to spread to the other lines. Ice castles and talking polar bears? Check. Underground cities populated by man-eating dark elves? Check. Baseball gnomes? Check.<br /> B k/nerd) if you never game, never go to the cons, never read another fantasy novel or watched another sci-fi show? That's the problem changelings face. Pretend too hard, and the lie becomes real.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> WOw I've been playing my mage games all wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T21:55:29-08:00","id":793422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=793276#post793276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WOw I've been playing my mage games all wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have <i>baseball </i>gnomes? Cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T23:18:29-08:00","id":793453,"title":"","content":"Changeling splats are known as kiths, and correspond to various types of faerie creatures. Born of different dreams and fantasies, each kith has been blessed by humanity with a particular gift, and a certain <i>style</i>:<ul><li>The <b>sidhe</b> are the Fair Folk, the Beautiful Ones. Knights and aristocrats, the sidhe are born of the dreams of nobility. The heroic champion in shining armor, the foul usurper who oppresses the masses, the rightful heir who returns to set things right . . . The sidhe find themselves exiled from the deathless lands of Arcadia, stranded in a world that believes the time for such heroics long passed.</li> <li>Travelers from afar, the <b>eshu</b> come bearing tales of distant wonders and epic deeds in exotic lands. Wandering storytellers and bards, an eshu always walks the path to adventure . . . whether they want to or not.</li> <li>Whisperers in the dark, the pale <b>sluagh</b> disturb even their (few) friends. Bend your ear close, and listen to their secrets . . . its better than having them seek you out. For a sluagh can <i>always</i> get to you, twisting and contorting into the most unnatural shapes to crawl under the door, or up through the pipes.</li> <li>Drawn from the myths of dwarves and goblins, the oft-surly <b>nockers</b> are the wondersmiths of the fae. An endless stream of treasures tumble from their forges: Thor's hammer Mjolnir or Freya's necklace, the sword Excalibur . . . with the right tools, a nocker can build anything from a mechanical dragon to steampunk mecha</li> </ul>Lusty satyrs and hardworking boggans, skin-changing selkies and mighty trolls . . . there are a wide variety of kiths to chose from. Throw in the Inanimae (dryads, mannequin people, and more), along with the Native American nunnehi and Asian hsien . . . players can take on the role of pretty much any creature from Eastern or Western mythology they want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=791411#post791411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .And the reason Technocracy (and everyone else) is able to mop up the floor with the Changelings because all the Changeling swords and dragons and rings of power aren't real. They are glamours, existing only in the Dreaming. A Changeling can spend some of his magic to materialized the items for a short time, but that comes with another set of problems. Changelings can do some scary and interesting things (Sidhe can run around with Appearance 10), but they burn out <i>very</i> quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why bother materializing anything? Between the memory-distorting Mists, and the sheer variety of chimera, the Dreaming practically begs for guerilla tactics. Enchant your foe, and <i>presto</i> - they're not in Kansas anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There's no reason in the world the changelings of Roswell can't stage an &quot;alien abduction&quot; (anal probing optional). Or drag their target off to &quot;Area 51&quot;, to be interrogated by &quot;real&quot; men-in-black. And you have to feel bad for the poor Prince who's retainers keep getting mugged by &quot;Robin Hood and his Merry Men&quot;. What's he supposed to do? Only <i>Malkavians</i> declare blood hunts on fictional characters!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: However, Onyx Path has also promised to beef up the faerie magic of changelings in the new edition, with a definite eye towards crossover potential. So if you absolutely <i>have</i> to slug it out with vampires/mages/etc., you'll have more options in C20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 12-27-2015, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T04:54:34-08:00","id":793517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=793422#post793422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have <i>baseball </i>gnomes? Cool!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not specifically, but how do you think the High and Middle Umbra act in relation to Sports Seasons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T10:06:45-08:00","id":793654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=793453#post793453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lusty satyrs</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Childlings are from 3 to 13 years old</div> </div> </div> </div>You can see why people are calling Changeling incredibly creepy. Loli sex goddess should not be a core archetype in any game one can talk in public. Satyrs/Nymphs/Apsara &quot;fairies as sex metaphor&quot; and the Peter Pan/Goblin King/Cottingley &quot;fairies as childhood metaphor&quot; both exist, but they shouldn't be in the same story, and they must never be in the same character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T10:21:48-08:00","id":793664,"title":"","content":"You know that Satyrs are creatures of passions and sex is just one of those potential passions that one can possess, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T10:58:28-08:00","id":793681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=793664#post793664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know that Satyrs are creatures of passions and sex is just one of those potential passions that one can possess, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changeling the Dreaming</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gift of Pan \u2014 Dionysian revelry is high ritual to these fae. Singing, music and dance can be used to stir fae and mortals alike to the height of <b>carnal passion</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The basic power every single satyr has (even the 3 y.o. ones) is the fuckmusic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T12:04:35-08:00","id":793713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=793681#post793681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The basic power every single satyr has (even the 3 y.o. ones) is the fuckmusic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect this will change in C20. The Adhene have different manifestations of their Birthrights at each Seeming already, so it could go that way. But most satyr players I know ignored the word 'carnal' in the write-up of that Birthright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-28-2015, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T05:30:22-08:00","id":794110,"title":"","content":"I suggest you search for the meaning of Carnal. It's not just sexual passion. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Adj.</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>1.</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>carnal</b> - marked by the appetites and passions of the body; &quot;animal instincts&quot;; &quot;carnal knowledge&quot;; &quot;fleshly desire&quot;; &quot;a sensual delight in eating&quot;; &quot;music is the only sensual pleasure without vice&quot;</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T09:36:50-08:00","id":794227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=794110#post794110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggest you search for the meaning of Carnal. It's not just sexual passion. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Adj.</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>1.</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>carnal</b> - marked by the appetites and passions of the body; &quot;animal instincts&quot;; &quot;carnal knowledge&quot;; &quot;fleshly desire&quot;; &quot;a sensual delight in eating&quot;; &quot;music is the only sensual pleasure without vice&quot;</td> </tr> </table></div></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not. But the first four definitions all allude to sexual passion. It's not till the fifth and sixth definitions that we see (some) divergence from that idea. <br /> <br /> It's a poor word choice, I agree, but I'd never read it to mean that satyrs can only cause people to (ahem) get the horn. I thought it was obvious that they can stir any passions in general, just as I always kinda understood that pooka don't literally have to lie about everything. <br /> <br /> Maybe this comes from wider reading than the core book, however. It is something that C20 should clean up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-31-2015, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T18:00:59-08:00","id":794508,"title":"","content":"Child satyrs are fully capable of driving people into childish fits of revelry rather than sexual fits of passion. &quot;Give in to your inner child&quot; or &quot;let loose your inner child&quot; type things. They can also take well-behaved, staid children and drive them to a frenzy of childish irresponsibility, making even the most uptight and well-behaved &quot;little adult&quot; act like a kid again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T03:52:30-08:00","id":794746,"title":"","content":"At this point, <b>AkatsukiLeader13</b>, do you (or does anyone else) have any particular questions about <b>Changeling</b>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=793517#post793517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not specifically, but how do you think the High and Middle Umbra act in relation to Sports Seasons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point . . . but that's the <i>Umbra</i>. Across the Gauntlet. There's no such barrier between the Dreaming and Earth, separating humans and chimera (the spirits of the Dreaming). Umbral spirits might play their own version of baseball, in the spiritual reflection of a stadium. But the baseball gnomes are actually <i>there</i>, at Wrigley Field or Shea Stadium. Hocking t-shirts, swearing at the refs, rubbing elbows with the humans* . . .<br /> <br /> So while the humans at BronyCon are snapping up souvenirs, and admiring the cosplay, the changeling attendees are taking selfies with Rainbow Dash and singing karaoke with the Sea Ponies. And there's no Paradox issue to trouble crossovers. A nocker can build a chimerical version of the Gundam Heavy Arms (giant anime mecha with machine gun arms), then use it to blow away a zombie horde in a <i>Walking Dead</i>-themed area of the Dreaming, while the dragon riders of Pern battle the (Wizard of Oz's) flying monkeys for control of Portland's skies.<br /> <br /> Such wild crossovers aren't mandatory . . . but they're an option here, in a way that they're not in <i>Mage</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *<i>this, of course, assumes the baseball gnomes are human-sized. Tiny gnomes that resemble baseballs, and who find it great fun to be thrown by pitchers, and sent flying by the batter, are also viable.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T13:01:38-08:00","id":795034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=794508#post794508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Child satyrs are fully capable of driving people into childish fits of revelry rather than sexual fits of passion. &quot;Give in to your inner child&quot; or &quot;let loose your inner child&quot; type things. They can also take well-behaved, staid children and drive them to a frenzy of childish irresponsibility, making even the most uptight and well-behaved &quot;little adult&quot; act like a kid again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and in Werewolf your character's parent can not be a dog rapist if you picked an origin that's not Lupus. But you know, the dog rape is still there. Just as loli sex goddess satyr is an emergent, and very disturbing, character archetype in Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T17:24:39-08:00","id":795218,"title":"","content":"Eh. If people want to take it that way, that's their issue/choice/hangup. You can make similar arguments about Vampire, given the presence of the Child flaw, and you can point to explicit text about one version of a Ventrue's &quot;picky eating&quot; to get the squickiness in black-and-white text, if you want.<br /> <br /> I sincerely doubt that the authors were picturing prepubescents as satyrs at all when they wrote the satyr racial power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T22:25:26-08:00","id":795395,"title":"","content":"It's fantasy. These things don't always make sense. Like, I sometimes reread Harry Potter and think, 'How on earth could Hagrid's mortal father inseminate a giant over 16 feet tall? How would his little dinky not just fall out of her epic womanhood?' etc, etc. Not to mention the odd relationship dynamics. But, you know, it's magic!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T16:02:05-08:00","id":797058,"title":"","content":"Baseball Gnomes totally sold me on Changeling...but is there anything like that in an actual changeling book? Does it have a City book or am I gonna have to build my own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T21:02:38-08:00","id":797175,"title":"","content":"The only city book I can think of is Immortal Eyes: The Toybox, which was one of the very first supplements and covers San Francisco. Other setting books are a little broader, with Immortal Eyes: Shadows on the Hill covering Hawaii, Immortal Eyes: Court of All Kings looking at Ireland, Kingdom of Willows being about the American South, and Isle of the Mighty being Great Britain. I've heard that last one isn't very good, but it's one of the few books I don't own so I can't say myself.<br /> <br /> Also, the entire Immortal Eyes trilogy, both the supplements and tie-in novels, is available as a $10 PDF addon in the Kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10165-flimflamberge","name":"Flimflamberge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T01:41:03-08:00","id":797233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flimflamberge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=797175#post797175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only city book I can think of is Immortal Eyes: The Toybox, which was one of the very first supplements and covers San Francisco. Other setting books are a little broader, with Immortal Eyes: Shadows on the Hill covering Hawaii, Immortal Eyes: Court of All Kings looking at Ireland, Kingdom of Willows being about the American South, and Isle of the Mighty being Great Britain. I've heard that last one isn't very good, but it's one of the few books I don't own so I can't say myself.<br /> <br /> Also, the entire Immortal Eyes trilogy, both the supplements and tie-in novels, is available as a $10 PDF addon in the Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know how in fantasy games you have locations that are fictionalized stereotypical versions of a nation but randomly thrown together bits out of time? That's what Isle of the Mighty is. It has just as much accuracy for the UK as Avalon from 7th Sea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T05:02:38-08:00","id":797280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=797233#post797233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You know how in fantasy games you have locations that are fictionalized stereotypical versions of a nation but randomly thrown together bits out of time? That's what Isle of the Mighty is. It has just as much accuracy for the UK as Avalon from 7th Sea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's wildly inaccurate. I was mostly annoyed that they said Yorkshire and Manchester were in the Midlands, however, when they're definitely considered The North by Brits. Still, it's nice we were noticed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T17:54:09-08:00","id":802504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=797058#post797058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baseball Gnomes totally sold me on Changeling...but is there anything like that in an actual changeling book? Does it have a City book or am I gonna have to build my own?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't an official build for them (although we did get steampunk goblins), but the first type of Baseball Gnome would be Boggans or Nockers (or possibly some of both), who belong to the Olympian clique. Cliques are the &quot;z-splat&quot; of the game, and revolve around preferred ways to pursue Glamour. And the Olympians pursue the Glamour born of sports dreams and the pursuit of physical perfection.<br /> <br /> If you really want to drive the idea home, go with a freehold (the changeling equivalent to a Node or Caern) with a strong baseball tie-in. Since freeholds are fueled by the dreams in that area, a stadium turned into a freehold (or the bar where the players used to celebrate, or . . . ) will become a veritable temple to the sport (at least within the Dreaming). The Hall of Fame pictures talk about past games, or give tips, people who break the rules of good sportsmanship get cursed . . .<br /> <br /> Kith plus clique plus freehold - the three combine to give you the exact nature of the dream your character represents. Boggans (gnomes/brownies), who wrap themselves in Glamour created by humans dreaming of a win for their team, and who control a baseball-themed freehold. Presto - instant Baseball Gnome<br /> <br /> Alternately, you could use redcaps or trolls . . . but I'd expect to see them in something more . . . full contact. Hockey or soccer or (American) football. Sports where their strength and aggressiveness gives them an advantage, and where they can indulge in a good post-game riot<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: For gnomes who look like baseballs, they could be a form of Inanimae - &quot;cousins&quot; to changelings, who bonded with inanimate objects instead of humans. Dryads, mannequin people, etc.<br /> <br /> Or they could be some of the local chimeras (the spirits of the Dreaming). Barring any special powers, PCs could buy them at character creation . . . Say, six baseball gnomes per background point,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 01-06-2016, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T17:42:07-08:00","id":805640,"title":"","content":"Just a reminder - if anyone's on the fence, the kickstarter's ending on Tuesday (at noon, Eastern). So there's less than forty eight hours to pledge, if you're interested. Stretch goals have already added a short story anthology and the &quot;missing&quot; Boggan kithbook, with more to come.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flimflamberge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=797175#post797175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only city book I can think of is Immortal Eyes: The Toybox, which was one of the very first supplements and covers San Francisco. Other setting books are a little broader, with Immortal Eyes: Shadows on the Hill covering Hawaii, Immortal Eyes: Court of All Kings looking at Ireland, Kingdom of Willows being about the American South, and Isle of the Mighty being Great Britain. I've heard that last one isn't very good, but it's one of the few books I don't own so I can't say myself.<br /> <br /> Also, the entire Immortal Eyes trilogy, both the supplements and tie-in novels, is available as a $10 PDF addon in the Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably worth mentioning <b>Freeholds and Hidden Glens</b>, too. Its a set of seven freeholds scattered across the United States. It doesn't go into much depth on the surrounding city, but it does touch on the nature of the local Dreaming.<br /> <br /> But here's a quick glance at some of the locations PCs can visit: <br /> <br /> <u><b>Graymere Glen</b></u>: From <i>Beowulf</i> to the <i>Friday the 13</i> movies, humanity has long told stories of the &quot;dark lake in the woods&quot;. They're all talking about the same place. They're talking about Dudleytown. <br /> <br /> No one really remembers what fell dream gave birth to the dark lake in the woods, but clearly it was a terrible one. Even the most banal Autumn Person can feel the fear etched in the local Dreaming, and for centuries, none would dare the woods. In search of tin, though, the men of Dudleytown dug up the surrounding hills, ignoring the warnings. And every night for a century, their children woke screaming, as the lake mined their nightmares for Glamour. <br /> <br /> Dudleytown has been a ghost town since the 1920s, but the freehold has lost not of its dark power. A place where the willows walk, and . . . <i>things</i> born of the children's nightmares still watch from the shadows. At night, the lake glows, and on the high holy days of the changeling calendar, it even freezes over (even in mid-summer), that the local changelings might dance upon the surface. Only a fool would dare touch the waters on any other day . . . but there have been many such fools over the years. Dragged beneath the surface by unseen hands, never to be seen again - locals whisper that the lake itself has taken them, to devour their souls.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Florist Primeval</b></u>: <i>One upon a time, a boy loved a girl who dreamt of flowers. And to win her heart, he promised to build her the garden of her dreams, hoping that would make her smile . . .</i><br /> <br /> Located in Savannna, Georgia, &quot;Florist Primeval&quot; is acres and acres of botanical gardens, greenhouses, and hedge mazes. The mundane world knows it as the headquarters of a premier florist and landscaping company. But as a freehold, the gardens of Florist Primeval are a favorite of local lovers, who come to flirt, picnic, and court among the blooms. <br /> <br /> As they wander the grounds, many sidhe experience flashbacks to Arcadia - which comes as no surprise, to those who know the story of the freehold. When both were college students, a human gardener fell for Lady Una Morrowind. And as his wedding gift to her, he built Florist Primeval from her memories of the gardens of the fabled fae realm. <br /> <br /> Now, in memory of her own romance, she watches over all the young lovers who visit Florist Primeval, turning none away. Seelie and Unseelie, human and fae . . . all are welcome to laugh and play among the gardens. <br /> <br /> Except for the unfinished hedge maze. That is hers, and hers alone. At night, she wanders through it, weeping softly. <br /> <br /> <i>Remembering how, once, a human boy had loved her. And just to see her smile, he built her a garden, grander than any in Arcadia. But only when it was too late, did she realize that she had loved him, too. </i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Goblin Town</b></u>: Located beneath the streets of a New York City, Goblin Town is no mere building. The underground freehold is actually a massive machine, a steampunk wonder sure to delight any Son of Ether. Every couple weeks, the entire place shifts into a different shape: halls and rooms and furniture sliding effortless , until it returns to its original shape on New Year's.<br /> <br /> Since its founding in the Nineteenth Century, the &quot;goblins&quot; (a group of Unseelie nockers) have worked relentlessly to expand the freehold, hoping that it will someday allow them to &quot;mine&quot; Glamour directly from the Dreaming itself. In the modern day, Goblin Town now extends under most of NYC, intertwined with the mundane subway and sewer systems. <br /> <br /> Besides expanding the great machine, the goblins like to dabble in intrigue. They know who <i>really</i> killed Lord Dafyll during the Accordance War, for example, and have their own plans for the future . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:11:50-08:00","id":806310,"title":"","content":"Yo everybody! Back after a long absence from the forums. Real Life and a rather crappy holiday will do that to someone.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I want to thank everyone for their feedback. I've decided to back C20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:08:19-08:00","id":806703,"title":"","content":"Yay! Welcome to the club.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T06:23:04-08:00","id":806951,"title":"","content":"You have also sold myself as well on it. For all the years I have collected and played White Wolf RPGs, it was the one that I never understood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4221-mrvyngaard","name":"MrVyngaard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4221_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T07:16:12-08:00","id":806989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrVyngaard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition?p=806951#post806951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have also sold myself as well on it. For all the years I have collected and played White Wolf RPGs, it was the one that I never understood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully that'll change. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyon